*HEADING
Young's modulus of a 50 % austenite + 50 % martensite mixture (27MnCr5)
** Units: mm, s, tonne, N, MPa, mJ, C
** KM: f_M = 1 - exp(-0.01 (372 - T)) = 0.5 at T = 372 - ln 2 / 0.01 = 302.7 C.
** Quench 1000 -> 303 C at 1000 C/s (no ferrite or bainite), hold, then 10 MPa along z:
** E_mix = 10 / dE33, to compare with 0.5 E_A(303) + 0.5 E_M(303) of the card (rule of mixtures
** expected from the hierarchical interpolation in the ratios r2-r4). The card gives austenite and
** martensite the same E near 300 C, so the discriminating check is the thermal strain THE33 at the
** hold: (fA alpha_A + fM alpha_M)(T - ZERO) - alpha_F(25)(25 - ZERO), against -2.4E-3 (pure A) and
** +5.7E-3 (pure M) in the 20MnCr5 card.
